This is a core work package. Start only after the named providers publish verified native/backend/persistence contracts and the package's implementation scope is authorized. Do not wait for an entire former numbered stage unless that contract acceptance is explicitly listed above. Do not use an unfinished sibling or mocked replacement as a hidden prerequisite.

## Delivered boundary

One complete native/Agent character workflow with independent structural/visual/calculated detail, safe LOD changes, offline and hosted recovery.

## Ownership and possible overlap

Character integration and resource acceptance; isolated performance sessions use the common measurement lane.

Independent ready packages may proceed together only after file/service ownership is reserved. Use separate leaf modules or isolated checkouts; shared migrations, command schemas, source/selection types, renderer lifetimes, runtime scheduling and performance sessions have one owner at a time. If actual code inspection finds an unproved shared boundary, add a dependency or serialize that work before coding. No promised worker count follows from the graph.

## Ordered work

Follow this package's task order. Original identifiers remain traceable; a reference to another former stage means its needed published contract, not an implicit global sequence. All native interaction, backend/persistence, authority, correctness and applicable resource obligations remain included.

### Task 11.T10

- [ ] **11.T10.** Implement independent anatomical coverage, display detail and calculation profile selection with shared demand/admission. Keep immutable source meshes/rig definitions/clips reusable, per-occurrence pose/controller state separate, bounds conservative across admitted poses and work proportional to visible/admitted active content. Validate LOD/source/rig/attachment replacement across representative poses before acceptance, release internal/high-detail geometry on last demand, and preserve already accepted motion constraints. Extend hosted sparse asset/presence/query paths for optional public appearance and private structure/annotations; a representation never grants physical interaction or participant-control authority.

### Task 11.T11

- [ ] **11.T11.** Deliver [B41](../contracts/Assembly-and-character-contracts.lingua#fixture-specifications-owned-here) end to end with native and Agent editing, save/reload/export, controller/clip/root-motion ownership, anatomy inspection, low-poly transition, hosted denial and source/rebind failure cases. Exercise the concrete shared-workflow recipes below and record unsupported operations explicitly. Keep added physical joint/muscle/tissue/cloth/hair predictions in stages 18–21; generic posing, fitting, geometric reach and semantic explanation remain usable without those calculations.

